comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T17:19:14.852Z","harness:claude-code","Blast radius measured 2026-07-26, and it just grew by three orders of magnitude.\n\nThe terminal relationship backfill added a typed implements edge from every closed or canceled item that has a parent to that parent — roughly 1,600 items — precisely because the scalar parent field is not a traversable semantic kind. The typed lineage now exists in the data. The traversal verbs still cannot see it.\n\nMeasured on pm-00yy, a closed item enriched by that pass: graph ancestors returns count 0 while reporting inspected_edges 10, so it walked the edges and accepted none of them. The same node under graph impact --direction outgoing --summary returns count 1444 with 9,568 edges inspected. One node, two traversal surfaces, and the difference between an empty answer and 1,444 reachable nodes is entirely which kinds the verb admits.\n\nBefore today this defect affected a few hundred active items whose typed edges were recently added. It now affects the whole terminal corpus, which is 86 percent of the workspace. Any agent that asks ancestors or predecessors what preceded a closed item gets zero and has no signal that the answer is a vocabulary artefact rather than a fact. That asymmetry — a confident empty result from one verb and a rich result from another over the same edges — is the part worth fixing first, ahead of any vocabulary expansion.\n\nOrdering note stands: pm-4020c5 must canonicalize the kind lexicon before these verbs widen, or the widening bakes in the alias spellings.\n"
  "2026-08-07T11:23:40.792Z","harness:claude-code","Confirmed still live at 2026.8.7, 2026-08-07. `pm graph predecessors pm-j82fd3 --kind implements` is refused with \"Relationship kind implements is not a ordering kind\" (exit 2). The consequence was measured this session: because no traversal verb accepts the semantic kinds, typed reachability to the outcome ladder had to be computed outside the product, by parsing the store directly. A governance invariant the project intends to enforce is therefore not expressible in the product that hosts it. Filed pm-h6b73t from that measurement. Minor secondary defect in the same message: the article reads \"a ordering kind\"."
  "2026-08-20T17:35:04.513Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-20: explicit kind filters on hierarchy and ordering verbs now admit registry-declared semantic kinds while unchanged calls retain the existing hierarchy-only or ordering-only defaults. Association kinds refuse with a graph impact --direction both recovery; structural family mismatches name the correct traversal verbs. The previously refused live probe pm graph predecessors pm-j82fd3 --kind implements now returns semantic predecessors with complete output metadata. Graph paths already supports kind filtering; scheduling slack and redundancy remain ordering-only by contract. Linked graph tests passed 155/155 and focused traversal/registry tests passed 34/34."
  "2026-08-20T17:37:44.962Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide verification 2026-08-20: pnpm test:coverage passed 539 files and 7,644 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; pnpm quality:static passed generated contracts, SDK surface, package parity, grammar, token budgets, tracker context, graph composition, record integrity, and transport floors; ESLint passed with zero warnings; jscpd found zero clones across 1,067 files; docs links passed; secret scan found no credential-like material; pnpm audit found no known vulnerabilities. Manual acceptance used a disposable initialized tracker and verified semantic traversal, duplicate collapse without edge absence, malformed removal refusal, and typed zero-match recovery."
  "2026-08-20T17:55:05.198Z","harness:codex","Hosted review remediation: classified the former live traversal refusal as a production_defect and recorded strengthened gate evidence covering opt-in semantic traversal, unchanged defaults, and incompatible-family negative controls."
  "2026-08-20T18:05:00.050Z","harness:codex","Hosted review follow-up: linked the exact relationship registry and traversal regression files and added an explicit hierarchy semantic-kind case alongside the ordering case. Focused verification will be rerun before push."
  "2026-08-20T18:38:41.320Z","harness:codex","Operational closeout 2026-08-20: broad delivery PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1067 merged to main as ff1554259dccc6c161ae8353ef039d04e34f6a83. Exact merged-main CI run 32403253005 passed build, Windows, four coverage shards plus exact coverage aggregation, static/typecheck/compat/smoke gates, runtime smokes, and release-analyzer provenance; CodeQL, security/script quality, OSSF Scorecard, docs, and CodSpeed also passed. Same-day policy preserved the sole v2026.8.20 release; verify-published-release passed npm metadata, npx, bunx, pm-mcp initialization, bin coverage, and missing-bin negative controls. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero high/critical Sentry issues, 2.36% seven-day finish error rate, and zero missing error-code rows. Inline dogfood telemetry drained one queued event with queue_progressed=true and queue_empty=true."
